    "id": "def:three-cell-five-arm-instance",
    "name": "Independent rational three-cell, five-arm instance",
    "construction": "Let \\(\\mathsf E_{3,5}\\) have \\(N=6\\), \\(\\mathcal X=\\{1,2,3\\}\\), \\((N_1,N_2,N_3)=(1,2,3)\\), \\((q_1,q_2,q_3)=(1/6,1/3,1/2)\\), \\(\\mathcal A=\\{0,1\\}\\), \\(a_0=0\\), \\(\\Gamma=1\\), and \\(k=2\\). Its future policies are \\(\\pi_1=(1,1,1)\\) with \\(m_{\\pi_1}=1/2\\) and \\(\\pi_2=(1,0,1)\\) with \\(m_{\\pi_2}=3/4\\). Its candidates are \\(c_1=(1,1,0)\\), \\(m_{c_1}=1/2\\); \\(c_2=(0,1,1)\\), \\(m_{c_2}=1/2\\); \\(c_3=(1,0,0)\\), \\(m_{c_3}=3/4\\); \\(c_4=(0,0,1)\\), \\(m_{c_4}=3/4\\); and \\(c_5=(0,1,0)\\), \\(m_{c_5}=1/4\\). For \\(S^{\\star}=\\{c_1,c_4\\}\\), fix \\(y_{c_1\\cdot}=(0,0,0)\\) and \\(y_{c_4\\cdot}=(0,0,1/4)\\). Define \\(\\mu^-_{x0}(t)=\\mu^+_{x0}(t)=0\\); for \\(x\\in\\{1,2\\}\\), define \\(\\mu^-_{x1}(t)=0\\) and \\(\\mu^+_{x1}(t)=(t-1/2)_+\\); and define \\(\\mu^-_{31}(t)=\\min\\{1/4,(t-1/2)_+\\}\\) and \\(\\mu^+_{31}(t)=1/4+(t-3/4)_+\\). For each unit in cell \\(x\\), set \\(Y_i(a,t)=\\mu^{\\pm}_{xa}(t)\\) to realize the corresponding fixed schedule.",
